# The aqueduct on the horizon, in silhouette. Tiles horizontally.
#
# Silhouette only — one colour, no interior detail. A parallax layer that shows
# its own shading competes with the foreground the player is standing on, and
# at this distance the eye reads shape and nothing else anyway.
#
# The arches are 40px across and the whole strip is 160, which is the fix for
# the version before it: small repeated arches read as a railing, not as
# architecture a mile away. Scale is what puts something in the distance —
# haze and detail-drop are for engines with more than one grey.
name platformer-ruins
size 160 64
key s stone-0-shadow
pixels
